ability-health-to-mana-summary = Spend up to { $cost } HP; gain actual HP lost divided by { $divisor } as mana, rounded down and capped at maximum mana. Full mana still costs HP; low HP can be fatal.
ability-mana-to-health-summary = Spend { $cost } mana to heal { $healing } base HP, subject to healing modifiers and maximum HP. Full HP still costs mana. Insufficient mana converts nothing and still spends a turn.
ability-resource-conversion-cost-help = The listed zero spell cost excludes the internal conversion payment above. A failed activation spends a turn without converting resources. The log shows actual HP and mana before and after conversion.
ability-bless-weapon-help = Select a weapon in your pack, equipment or at your feet. Cancelling costs no time or resources. Curses or weapon properties can block blessing; resistance may reduce enchantments. Success reveals only the blessing and sets a 99% discount.
ability-evocation-summary = Dispel damage { $damage } · fear and teleport power { $power }. Each stage affects surviving monsters within line of sight and effect. Casting still costs resources with no targets.
ability-priest-blade-penalty = Current edged weapons add { $value } percentage points to prayer failure. Each spell shows its final failure chance.
ability-priest-blade-unknown = Some weapons have unknown blessing properties, so their prayer penalty is unknown. Each spell shows its final failure chance.
trait-stat-priest-blade-failure = Edged weapon prayer penalty
trait-priest-blade-rule = Each unblessed sword or polearm gives a good Priest -2 to hit and damage and adds 25 percentage points to prayer failure. Blessing removes these penalties. Evil Priests are exempt. Only known sources are listed here.
