trait-weapon-selection-rule = Equipped weapons attack separately with their own damage, slays and brands. Dual-wield accuracy depends on proficiency and weapon weight; Genji gloves improve it. Draconian metamorphosis replaces weapon attacks with innate attacks.
trait-launcher-selection-rule = Shooting uses the selected launcher and compatible ammunition. This modifier belongs to this launcher, not every weapon.
trait-attack-rates = Attack count and shot rate
trait-stat-melee-attacks-hundredths = Regular melee attacks
trait-melee-damage = Base damage per hit
trait-melee-damage-range = { $minimum }–{ $maximum }
trait-melee-damage-percent = Racial melee damage multiplier: { $value }%
trait-melee-damage-rule = Includes damage bonuses and the racial multiplier, rounded per hit. Excludes criticals, slays, triggered effects and target resistance. The range stays unknown until equipment is fully identified.
trait-stat-ranged-base-shot = Base shot rate
trait-stat-ranged-energy = Energy per shot
trait-unarmed = No weapon source
trait-unit-attacks = { $value } attacks / melee action
trait-unit-energy = { $value } energy
trait-melee-rate-rule = Read directly from the regular melee profile. The fractional part is the chance of one extra attack: 1.96 means one attack plus a 96% chance of another. The minimum is 0.00. Sources show effective adjustments; innate attacks and action-specific techniques are excluded. Totals affected by unidentified equipment are withheld.
trait-shot-rate-rule = Taken from the selected launcher's core projectile profile. Base shot rate and energy cost determine firing frequency, not automatic extra projectiles per command. This page does not reverse-engineer hidden contributions.
trait-auras = Contact auras
trait-aura-fire = Fire aura
trait-aura-electricity = Electricity aura
trait-aura-cold = Cold aura
trait-aura-holy = Contact retaliation (evil targets only)
trait-contact-scope = Character contact retaliation
trait-aura-rule = Triggered by qualifying enemy contact attacks, not added to every weapon attack. Targets with ordinary/strong resistance or immunity skip that elemental retaliation. Overlapping timed sources are combined by the core. Damage is not estimated here.
trait-holy-aura-rule = Retaliates after qualifying contact attacks only against evil targets without resist-all, using the core mana-damage path. It is not a global melee damage brand.
trait-no-auras = No currently active projected contact auras.
trait-negatives = Curses and known negative effects
trait-no-confirmed-curse = No confirmed curse
trait-curse-effect-aggravate = Aggravate monsters
trait-curse-stealth-penalty = Aggravation converted to a stealth penalty
trait-curse-effect-teleport = Random teleport
trait-curse-rule-aggravate = The equipped effect is enabled under current rules. A qualifying fairy racial trait converts it to a stealth penalty instead of waking monsters.
trait-curse-rule-teleport = Checked periodically, not an immediate teleport. Certain intrinsic teleport effects are suppressed when uncursed and inscribed with a period; the environment can still prevent teleportation.
trait-curse-severity-rule = The heading is known curse severity only. Effects apply to the character, not just this weapon's attacks. Active means the source is enabled, not that it triggers every turn. Only independently known, implemented effects are listed; severity does not imply others.
trait-no-negatives = No revealed curses or projected negative effects; unknown equipment may still have negative properties.
